<title>BELGIUM: EU prepared to brief Clinton on EMU.</title>
<headline>EU prepared to brief Clinton on EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union officials on Tuesday said they were prepared to brief U.S. president Bill Clinton on Europe's planned single currency when he arrives in the Netherlands on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Clinton, who will take part in celebrations marking the 50th anniversary of U.S. aid to a war-ravaged Europe, will meet European Commission president Jacques Santer to discuss a wide range of foreign policy issues.</p>
<p>Although U.S. officials said economic and monetary union (EMU) was not on the official agenda, EU officials said they were ready to answer any questions Clinton might have on developments in the single currency.</p>
</text>
